  "interface": {
    "entry": "demlik_tea::agent::status(&AgentState) -> ProjectedStatus, with all existing state slots inferred and no opaque Clone/serde/Send/static bounds.",
    "closedStatus": "AgentStatus::Idle / Running / Suspended{pending:&Vec<Rc<ToolCall>>} / Ended(AgentEndedStatus). The existing terminal owner remains the only Done/Failed/Cancelled declaration; nested exhaustive matches cover all six logical arms.",
    "terminalFailure": "AgentTerminalFailure::Agent(original Rc<AgentFailure<FE>>) or Run(original Rc<RunFailure<Stage,SE>>). The sum carrier wraps the existing records rather than reconstructing failure facts; original stage/cause handles remain accessible.",
    "minimalEndedRepair": "Done.output is AgentField<Option<Rc<T>>>; Failed.failure is AgentField<Rc<F>>; Cancelled.at is canonical AgentNumber/NumberOrNull. Pure status creates Undefined for a missing/undefined read and preserves explicit output null. Conditional serialization stays flat and omits undefined fields.",
    "borrowedPending": "Suspended exposes the original Vec header, including distinct empty collection identity. A caller retaining that view keeps its immutable state owner alive while advancing another state. It is not an independently owned pending-array promise. Moving an Ended value out retains its original terminal handles after dropping the state.",
    "laws": [
      "Agent annotation, including missing/undefined, wins before every run phase. A late brain failure after cancellation projects failed while the run remains cancelled.",
      "Explicit null annotation falls through the exhaustive phase match: idle, failed original monitored-run cause, done, cancelled, running/stale.",
      "Done preserves original output/usage handles. Nullish usage uses the existing shared NO_USAGE; no state migration, conversation-usage lifting, zero reminting or validation occurs.",
      "Running/stale with awaiting tools projects suspended using tools.running, even when empty. Compaction awaiting remains running.",
      "Cancelled preserves stored nullable/nonfinite/signed-zero/fractional time without arithmetic coercion."
    ],
    "lint": "One function-scoped expect(clippy::type_complexity), justified by the fourteen unconstrained canonical state slots and an inferred one-reference call. No projection trait or global lint change."
